      "body": "- `embedding_gemma2.py`, `diffusion_gemma.py`: copy Gemma4's `_get_max_soft_tokens` alongside the `_process_image_input` they already borrow\n\n#60687 moved the `max_soft_tokens` lookup into a new `Gemma4ForConditionalGeneration._get_max_soft_tokens` helper that `_process_image_input` now calls. `EmbeddingGemma2Model` and `DiffusionGemmaForConditionalGeneration` copy `_process_image_input` as a class attribute but not the helper, so `test_embedding_gemma2.py::test_encoder_contract` has failed since it merged, on AMD and NVIDIA ([build 97017](https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/97017/list?jid=01a16cae-f374-4a87-b95b-517c63fda082&tab=output)). The call only runs with tower-connector LoRA enabled, which neither model supports yet, so today it is a latent `AttributeError` that #60632 would turn into a real one. DiffusionGemma has the same gap but no contract test.\n\n`test_encoder_contract` fails on main and passes 10/10 with this change; reverting only #60687's `gemma4_mm.py` hunk on main also makes it pass.\n\nAI assistance (Claude Code) was used to draft this change. Every line was reviewed by the submitter.\n\n\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/vllm-project/codesmith/vllm/pr/63538?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3-3x.png\" width=\"162\" height=\"28\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1795491219&installation_model_id=425286&pr_number=63538&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=vllm-project%2Fvllm&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fvllm-project%2Fvllm%2Fpull%2F63538&signature=5fe0e15a